== ItemValue.xml
== Fixed sell-price / zen value table for items that don't
== use the normal formula-based pricing (event/cash items,
== jewel bundles, potions, etc).
== Loaded by GameServer via CItemValue::LoadXML().
==
== NOTE: the original ItemValue.txt only ever had 4 real
== columns (Index/Level/Grade/Value) even though the C++
== struct/Load() historically read 8 fields per record
== (...,Coin1,Coin2,Coin3,Sell). Because the legacy parser
== reads tokens as one continuous stream ignoring line
== breaks, this silently misaligned every record - each
== item's Coin1/Coin2/Coin3/Sell were actually the NEXT
== line's Index/Level/Grade/Value. This was a real bug in
== the live server (confirmed 2026-08-25). LoadXML() fixes
== this: it reads exactly the 4 fields below per item, and
== Coin1/Coin2/Coin3/Sell now default to 0 for every entry.
== Modify only if you know what you're doing!
============================================================

### ItemValue::Config ###
	Index    Item index (Section*512 + SubIndex encoding, matches
	         Item.txt/Item.xml's raw index values, not GET_ITEM()).
	Level    Required item +Level for this price to apply. -1 = any.
	Grade    Required item Grade/NewOption byte for this price to
	         apply (used for items like Horn of Dinorant where the
	         grade encodes which mount). -1 = any.
	Value    Zen sell price (or coin price where relevant).
	Comment  Free-text label, for readability only.

STRICTLY NO COMMENTS INSIDE TAGS
-->

